<title>BAHRAIN: Arab Insurance Group lifts '96 net profit 16 pct.</title>
<headline>Arab Insurance Group lifts '96 net profit 16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			 (million U.S. dollars, rounded)</p>
<p> Net profit		   42.36     vs    36.58</p>
<p> Pre-tax			47.56     vs    40.87</p>
<p> Underwriting income	40.47     vs    33.07</p>
<p> Investment income	  37.19     vs    35.34</p>
<p> Proposed total dividend  18.00     vs    15.00</p>
<p> Assets			886.59     vs   828.44</p>
<p>Full Name: Arab Insurance Group.</p>
<p>Note - The Bahrain-based firm is one of the Arab world's largest insurance companies. It is owned by the governments of Kuwait, the United Arab Emirates and Libya.</p>
</text>
